29,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Transport costs vary wildly depending on distance, and whole-building lets have strict non-refundable deposits based on a fixed headcount. We need to be careful about how we handle late cancellations.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The inland centers seem risky; other clubs reported eight people to a room and strict curfews. Also, attendance sheets show a fifth of members skip away camps entirely, often leaving the club shortly after.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The campus canteen closes during vacation, meaning we'd have to cook for ourselves, which took two hours a day last year. Also, public bookings require a complex lottery and a nine-page application.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Public beds are quite cheap at 1,100 yen per night, but a third of our members can't even reach campus by 9 AM without paying for a bed the night before.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The seniors say mixing only happens when everyone sleeps in the same place. Also, the club hall is already booked by three other clubs, so our training would be split into weird hours.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the hall is that crowded and the seniors say shared sleeping is key for bonding, staying on campus seems like a poor choice for both training and social goals.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, I agree. Between the poor attendance at away camps and the cramped conditions inland, we need a balance. But if we go too far, the transport costs Asuka mentioned will be a problem.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, if public beds are so cheap, maybe that helps with the budget? But the nine-page application and lottery sound really stressful for whoever has to do the paperwork.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"The cheap rates are a plus, but @Minato is right about the stress. If the application is that rigid, any small change in our plans could force us to start the whole process over.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly. If we're stuck with weird training hours on campus and the inland spots are just cramped dorms, we need something that actually lets us bond without killing the organizers.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, since you mentioned that a fifth of members skip away camps, we have to consider if a distant location is even viable, regardless of the bonding potential.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"It's a valid point. If we choose a place too far, we might lose a significant portion of the membership, which defeats the purpose of a club training camp.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, if we go somewhere with a fixed headcount and non-refundable deposits, what happens if those people don't show up? Does the club have to pay for them?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"That's exactly the problem. If the deposit is non-refundable and based on a fixed headcount, the club account would likely have to cover the gap for any late dropouts.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"That's a nightmare. We can't let the club account take the hit again. If we want everyone to actually bond and show up, we need a place that's accessible but still lets us stay together.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"It seems we are caught between a rock and a hard place. We need a location that encourages bonding and minimizes administrative burden, but we cannot risk further financial instability or low attendance.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"If we avoid the inland centers due to the sleeping conditions and the campus due to the schedule, we're left with something more private, provided we can manage the risk of cancellations.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just don't want anyone to spend their whole camp cooking or doing paperwork. If we can find a place with staff to handle the meals, it would be much better for everyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree with Minato. Reducing the burden on the organizers is just as important as the budget. We need a destination that doesn't sacrifice the training or the people running it.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"We've ruled out the campus hall and the cramped inland dorms. If we want real bonding and no cooking duties, a private lodge seems like the only way, as long as we're smart about the money.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
